    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that {@link StrSubstitutor} can produce output identical to its input. <p>The interesting case here is a self-referential substitution. With {@code animal = \"$${${thing}}\"} and {@code thing = \"animal\"}, expanding {@code ${animal}} yields {@code \"$${animal}\"}; the {@code $$} then collapses to a literal {@code $}, giving back {@code \"${animal}\"}. So the template {@code \"The ${animal} jumps.\"} substitutes to itself.</p>"
   },
   {
